course: dictionary
lesson: 9214
title: Solo: one person alone
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A solo is something done by one person alone, with no one else helping or joining in. Solo can be a noun, an adjective or an adverb, but the meaning stays the same: by yourself.
explain: In a concert, a pupil who sings a solo sings alone while the others listen. «Teachers often give a solo to the child most ready for that piece.» The clue is that one child is picked for the piece, so solo must mean one person on their own.
explain: In everyday life, going solo means doing something by yourself. «She sailed solo round the world.» Sailing round the world alone is a big job for one person, so solo here means alone.
fact: Solo means done by one person alone, without help.
fact: A solo can be a piece of music, a dance or a performance done by one person.
fact: «Go solo» and «fly solo» mean doing something by yourself.
fact: «Jazz players make up solos on the spot after years of practice.»
fact: Solo can be a noun, an adjective or an adverb, depending on how it is used in the sentence.
exercise: «Teachers often give a solo to the child most ready for that piece.» What is a solo here? | A room where the choir practises | A group of children singing together | A teacher who plays the piano | *A piece of music sung or played by one person alone
exercise: Ella says, «I will fly solo on my first flight lesson.» What does fly solo mean? | *Fly by yourself, with no one else on board | Fly very high in the sky | Not fly at all | Fly in a big group with friends
exercise: «She made a solo trip to the shops.» In this sentence, what kind of word is solo? | An adverb | A verb | *An adjective, describing the trip | A noun
test: Ben played a guitar solo at the concert. What is a guitar solo? | A quiet lesson about guitars | *A part of a song played by one player alone | A guitar that is broken | A song sung by the whole band
test: «Mia sailed solo round the world.» What does solo mean here? | *Alone | With her family | In a race with other boats | Very fast
exam: Which sentence uses solo as an adverb? | She sang a solo at the school concert | The solo dancer bowed to the crowd | *Mia wanted to fly solo across the lake | Her solo trip took three days
